{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo","id":560314,"title":"New Conspiracy: The Otodo","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-18T21:03:44-07:00","id":560314,"title":"New Conspiracy: The Otodo","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/dark-eras-hunter-edo-jidai-preview/\" target=\"_blank\">Check them out here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:09:51-07:00","id":560339,"title":"","content":"Kaibutsu now officially replaces Mark of the Beast in my home games. It justdoes.<br /> <br /> Actually, even if I don't use the Otodo themselves, their Endowment helps update <i>a lot</i> of what made Castigation stupidly good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:25:49-07:00","id":560347,"title":"","content":"I need to actually read this in detail later, but on a quick skim the Otodo seem quite interesting.<br /> <br /> Though the first thing that jumps out to me is the statement in the Kanabo description that cold iron deals aggravated damage to Changelings. That's new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:29:41-07:00","id":560353,"title":"","content":"Looks pretty good to me. I'm looking forward to a lot of the stuff in this one and keeping my fingers crossed for a look at the period that's better researched than...certain other depictions of Japan from the past while still leaving wiggle room for supernatural shenanigans. I really hope we get teppou and yari as well as katana.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:32:47-07:00","id":560354,"title":"","content":"Wow, this looks totally awesome. I dig the group ideas listed in that post, and it feels like they hit a lot of the notes players would be interested in (shout out to the pearl divers, that's a cool surprise.)<br /> <br /> I know that redlines and stuff are exactly the place where this sort of thing gets fixed: I dig the Beast reference under Iron Clubs, but I feel like it's sort of weird to put it there? I'm honestly at a loss for where else to put it, but it doesn't feel like it has much to do with the sidebar, as it were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 06-19-2015, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:40:22-07:00","id":560359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560353#post560353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks pretty good to me. I'm looking forward to a lot of the stuff in this one and keeping my fingers crossed for a look at the period that's better researched than...certain other depictions of Japan from the past while still leaving wiggle room for supernatural shenanigans. I really hope we get teppou and yari as well as katana.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. I hope to please. I know the topic pretty well, and live here. So I have some great resources to draw from. <br /> <br /> If I do weapons (and I might, not sure yet), I'm also including guns. Because at this point, they were dominant weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:44:28-07:00","id":560363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560347#post560347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need to actually read this in detail later, but on a quick skim the Otodo seem quite interesting.<br /> <br /> Though the first thing that jumps out to me is the statement in the Kanabo description that cold iron deals aggravated damage to Changelings. That's new.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I'm still 50/50 on it. I prefer to have weaknesses inherit. And the cold iron weakness in Lost 1e is kind of lackluster, because it only applies to specific characters using specific powers, and even then, it only negates those advantages. To me, that's kinda boring as a weakness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:50:00-07:00","id":560366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560359#post560359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well. I hope to please. I know the topic pretty well, and live here. So I have some great resources to draw from.<br /> <br /> If I do weapons (and I might, not sure yet), I'm also including guns. Because at this point, they were dominant weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glorious. I'll be keeping my fingers crossed for 'em. If nothing else a nice firm reminder that this is Japan and not Rokugan will be much much appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:50:38-07:00","id":560367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560363#post560363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I'm still 50/50 on it. I prefer to have weaknesses inherit. And the cold iron weakness in Lost 1e is kind of lackluster, because it only applies to specific characters using specific powers, and even then, it only negates those advantages. To me, that's kinda boring as a weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Will Dark Eras be using Changeling 1e or 2e rules?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:55:38-07:00","id":560369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560367#post560367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Will Dark Eras be using Changeling 1e or 2e rules?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>2e. In fact, I'm introducing a seventh Seeming in one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T21:57:43-07:00","id":560371,"title":"","content":"Okay, so looking through the powers now. First of all, awesome description of like the scars and stuff from changing their powers around, that's super cool.<br /> <br /> Are high Status Rampant effectively immortal, like the Lady of Milan or Chevalier Theleme?<br /> <br /> Dorei-sei, I think the mechanics are a little iffy, if not just the idea that you need to get successes equal to a certain number to beat it. That's sort of lame with how everything else has mostly stuck to the success = regular success stuff. Maybe the dots in Seikotusen count as a penalty to the roll? I dunno, but I'd prefer not to do that mechanic. It's fiddly, I guess?<br /> <br /> Hannya is cool, seems fine to me.<br /> <br /> Kaibutsu is pretty cool, and I think it's interesting that higher Integrity makes it easier to use, not sure if I like that. Seeing as its an extended action, multiple successes makes sense to me, though it also might make it less cool if it takes awhile to activate it. Just my 2 cents, people like their transformation powers quick &amp; cool.<br /> <br /> Kenshi is awesome. The Rampant are scary effective banishers of Ephemeral Beings, it seems. Awesome.<br /> <br /> Kigo is a cool and interesting power. It reminds me of a power Sanctified could use in 1e Theban Sorcery, neat.<br /> <br /> Shinigami Buki is pretty devastating. You could see why other Hunters might be horrified if they do that willy nilly. Making them Thralls? Damn, that's mean.<br /> Shonetsu Jigoku is pure cool.<br /> <br /> I think I'd convert these for nu-Castigation if I played a Hunter game where Lucifuge were in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:05:43-07:00","id":560394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560369#post560369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2e. In fact, I'm introducing a seventh Seeming in one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks. When is the general time frame for release of Changeling 2e and Dark Eras? Since I assume Mage and Promethean 2e are earlier in the queue, will we have to wait until late 2016 or 2017?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:11:33-07:00","id":560397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560394#post560394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Thanks. When is the general time frame for release of Changeling 2e and Dark Eras? Since I assume Mage and Promethean 2e are earlier in the queue, will we have to wait until late 2016 or 2017?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless there's some unexpected hiccups, I'm going to say Changeling should definitely be out this year. We have solid first drafts. I'm in the middle of revising them; they're a great foundation.<br /> <br /> I have no idea about Dark Eras. I wrote one of them, and I'm developing a couple expansions. I don't have much insight on the higher level stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:11:37-07:00","id":560398,"title":"","content":"Please, <i>please</i> tell me pearl divers mean we'll be seeing some Deep Ones in the World of Darkness. Aquatic beasties don't get nearly enough love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:12:08-07:00","id":560399,"title":"","content":"Some of the dice pool mechanics are bit wonky. Resistance Pools requiring to exceed a static number is fairly uncommon and Hannya essentially has its own unique form for a clash of wills. (I'm assuming based on the Integrity references that 2.0 rules are in full effect).<br /> <br /> Overall I like the piece though, lots of obvious parallels to the lucifuge despite the disparate culture, and the changeling thing adding a strange wrinkle to their world-view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:14:58-07:00","id":560400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560398#post560398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, <i>please</i> tell me pearl divers mean we'll be seeing some Deep Ones in the World of Darkness. Aquatic beasties don't get nearly enough love.</div> </div> </div> </div>The plan is to add some of them. I referenced some in Werewolf 2e; I figure this Compact's a great place to go at them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:16:03-07:00","id":560401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560398#post560398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, <i>please</i> tell me pearl divers mean we'll be seeing some Deep Ones in the World of Darkness. Aquatic beasties don't get nearly enough love.</div> </div> </div> </div>*looks sideways at the Makara*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:20:36-07:00","id":560406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560401#post560401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*looks sideways at the Makara*</div> </div> </div> </div>No neat little boxes...there can be more.<br /> *Hides numerous Makara character ideas*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:23:56-07:00","id":560428,"title":"","content":"The MM is here? Wasn't expecting that. Makes sense, though.<br /> <br /> Overall looks pretty cool. The Rampant are pretty interesting and the other Compact/Conspiracy blurbs have me wanting to hear more about them, too. Also, glad you went with Edo, if memory serves the era was pretty much set up to go either Edo or Sengoku if it needed to.<br /> <br /> Is this going to be before or after the isolationism laws kicked in?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560363#post560363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I'm still 50/50 on it. I prefer to have weaknesses inherit. And the cold iron weakness in Lost 1e is kind of lackluster, because it only applies to specific characters using specific powers, and even then, it only negates those advantages. To me, that's kinda boring as a weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm 50-50 on the idea as well. 1E Changelings never really felt like they needed a weakness to me. Like it makes sense for Werewolves and Vampires because they're harder to kill, but if you shoot a Changeling they tend to die. They were a bit like Mages in that regard. Yeah you could game a Changeling really hard and make a tank, but for the most part they were fairly low on the superpower spectrum. I guess it just depends how much 2E's overall power creep/boost/whatever has affected them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:42:55-07:00","id":560433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560428#post560428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The MM is here? Wasn't expecting that. Makes sense, though.<br /> <br /> Overall looks pretty cool. The Rampant are pretty interesting and the other Compact/Conspiracy blurbs have me wanting to hear more about them, too. Also, glad you went with Edo, if memory serves the era was pretty much set up to go either Edo or Sengoku if it needed to.<br /> <br /> Is this going to be before or after the isolationism laws kicked in?.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's still AD 1600, it should be before. I do hope it is because I think the looming threat of Sekigahara makes a *glorious* backdrop. Especially with that compact of samurai who hunt down supernaturals lurking amidst the upper echelons (which reminds me rather pleasingly of Onimusha, after a fashion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:43:59-07:00","id":560435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560428#post560428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The MM is here? Wasn't expecting that. Makes sense, though.<br /> <br /> Overall looks pretty cool. The Rampant are pretty interesting and the other Compact/Conspiracy blurbs have me wanting to hear more about them, too. Also, glad you went with Edo, if memory serves the era was pretty much set up to go either Edo or Sengoku if it needed to.<br /> <br /> Is this going to be before or after the isolationism laws kicked in?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm 50-50 on the idea as well. 1E Changelings never really felt like they needed a weakness to me. Like it makes sense for Werewolves and Vampires because they're harder to kill, but if you shoot a Changeling they tend to die. They were a bit like Mages in that regard. Yeah you could game a Changeling really hard and make a tank, but for the most part they were fairly low on the superpower spectrum. I guess it just depends how much 2E's overall power creep/boost/whatever has affected them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I figure the Malleus showed up in the very early 17th century, when the Netherlands and Japan established trade relations. The Dutch helped to quell the Japanese Christian uprisings, which I figure was a matter of ideological purity for the Malleus. The Malleus doesn't maintain a strong presence in Edo in the period, but enough of one that others pay attention. <br /> <br /> It's taking place shortly after the isolationism laws took place. We're aiming for the 1640s. And yeah, I went with Edo because I didn't really want to make it about the Battle of Sekigahara. I'm not too interested in war stuff, but the aftermath is really great for Hunter stories. Basically, this is in the shift to the Tokugawa Shogunate, when there's a huge push to purify all the outside influence out of Japan. I figure that's got to be a metaphor for Hunter if there ever was one, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:51:08-07:00","id":560441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560435#post560435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's taking place shortly after the isolationism laws took place. We're aiming for the 1640s. And yeah, I went with Edo because I didn't really want to make it about the Battle of Sekigahara. I'm not too interested in war stuff, but the aftermath is really great for Hunter stories. Basically, this is in the shift to the Tokugawa Shogunate, when there's a huge push to purify all the outside influence out of Japan. I figure that's got to be a metaphor for Hunter if there ever was one, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, that's a slight pity, but the reasoning is understandable. I was kind of hoping it would be early in 1600 and that there'd be samurai Compact whose fealties would end up putting them on the LOSING side of Sekigahara, with a theme of being caught between their duty to uphold the Vigil and their duty to clans they'd be vassals to. Potentially ending the way a lot of jidaigeki do--in gore-stained tragedy. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:52:57-07:00","id":560443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CycloneJoker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560441#post560441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm, that's a slight pity, but the reasoning is understandable. I was kind of hoping it would be early in the year and that there'd be samurai Compact whose fealties would end up putting them on the LOSING side of Sekigahara, with a theme of being caught between their duty to uphold the Vigil and their duty to clans they'd be vassals to. Potentially ending the way a lot of jidaigeki do--in gore-stained tragedy. XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? A big part of that is, I didn't want to give undue weight to samurai. Fetishism issues aside, I prefer your everyday people. I almost didn't include samurai in this piece at all, but I felt I had an interesting spin on them that you don't really get to see in games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T22:59:51-07:00","id":560445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560443#post560443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly? A big part of that is, I didn't want to give undue weight to samurai. Fetishism issues aside, I prefer your everyday people. I almost didn't include samurai in this piece at all, but I felt I had an interesting spin on them that you don't really get to see in games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I look forward to it. I also don't particularly care for the pop culture interpretation of samurai all that much, especially the 80s-style fetishism (and do not even get me *started* about ninja). But I actually love the real history that went on with them--I do have to confess that I find the era's military history to be exceedingly fascinating and was kind of hoping I'd get to strap on a suit of <i>tosei-gusoku</i> and kick a bit of monster ass as a fully-trained and battle-hardened member of a military aristocracy in its prime. XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T23:13:49-07:00","id":560448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560371#post560371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kaibutsu is pretty cool, and I think it's interesting that higher Integrity makes it easier to use, not sure if I like that. Seeing as its an extended action, multiple successes makes sense to me, though it also might make it less cool if it takes awhile to activate it. Just my 2 cents, people like their transformation powers quick &amp; cool.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Given how Integrity works, that could be harnessing your Oni side safely rather than letting it rampage all Shonen Evil Badass Split Personality like.<br /> <br /> I also have a very good idea of what dramatic failure for that looks like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T00:03:42-07:00","id":560497,"title":"","content":"So those unseen senses they gain at level five- it's worded a little ambiguously to me. I assume it means unseen senses- everything like a mage, but one could argue it could also mean that the oniblooded is capable of choosing what monster their unseen senses can detect. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T00:13:04-07:00","id":560499,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed the writeup. It presented an interesting view of the 7th Generation in places before Christianity took root. It also seems that the Rampant are, apparently, not among the 12 races the changeling send ambassadors to, which can narrow the list a bit. Another surprising feature is that they hunt Beasts down- since that according to Beast, the Begotten have some sort of an alliance with the Rampant against the Heroes- I assume the Dawn of Heroes and the Guilds were created in a latter time?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure, but the way they see the MM may indicate that their Endowments don't work in Japan of that Era. Sure, I assume I read too much into the text, but if this is true it may have some interesting implications about the nature of their powers. The other groups also seems kinda interesting- the Ama San seem to be like a mariner, sea monster hunting version of the Union, and for some reason they make me think about epic fisherman who fights to fish a Japanese dragon out of the sea :P. I personally don't find the Gimu really attractive, but this is because samurais aren't really my shtick- but I think they present a very interesting mirror to the TF:V of the time and the place. The Bijin interest me because male escorts who hunt monsters is just awesome, and while I've made a similar group once I'm interesting in seen how those guys may end up. Finally, the Hototogisu- I think that among the different Japanese groups, they are the greatest power to reckon with. I wonder how tied they are to the tradition on the Onmyodo, since I've made a group of onmyoji hunters with a twist once and I wonder if I'll have to revise them...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I eagerly wait for the full Dark Era! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T00:22:10-07:00","id":560503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560499#post560499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really enjoyed the writeup. It presented an interesting view of the 7th Generation in places before Christianity took root. It also seems that the Rampant are, apparently, not among the 12 races the changeling send ambassadors to, which can narrow the list a bit. Another surprising feature is that they hunt Beasts down- since that according to Beast, the Begotten have some sort of an alliance with the Rampant against the Heroes- I assume the Dawn of Heroes and the Guilds were created in a latter time?<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure, but the way they see the MM may indicate that their Endowments don't work in Japan of that Era. Sure, I assume I read too much into the text, but if this is true it may have some interesting implications about the nature of their powers. The other groups also seems kinda interesting- the Ama San seem to be like a mariner, sea monster hunting version of the Union, and for some reason they make me think about epic fisherman who fights to fish a Japanese dragon out of the sea :P. I personally don't find the Gimu really attractive, but this is because samurais aren't really my shtick- but I think they present a very interesting mirror to the TF:V of the time and the place. The Bijin interest me because male escorts who hunt monsters is just awesome, and while I've made a similar group once I'm interesting in seen how those guys may end up. Finally, the Hototogisu- I think that among the different Japanese groups, they are the greatest power to reckon with. I wonder how tied they are to the tradition on the Onmyodo, since I've made a group of onmyoji hunters with a twist once and I wonder if I'll have to revise them...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I eagerly wait for the full Dark Era! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that alliance happens later.<br /> <br /> So far, I don't reference the Onmyodo in the Hototogisu writeup, mostly because the two haven't really converged yet. The modern Hototogisu is almost indistinguishable from its ancient counterpart. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560497#post560497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So those unseen senses they gain at level five- it's worded a little ambiguously to me. I assume it means unseen senses- everything like a mage, but one could argue it could also mean that the oniblooded is capable of choosing what monster their unseen senses can detect.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll clarify; it's supposed to be Unseen Sense: Everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T00:32:52-07:00","id":560506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560499#post560499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really enjoyed the writeup. It presented an interesting view of the 7th Generation in places before Christianity took root. It also seems that the Rampant are, apparently, not among the 12 races the changeling send ambassadors to, which can narrow the list a bit. Another surprising feature is that they hunt Beasts down- since that according to Beast, the Begotten have some sort of an alliance with the Rampant against the Heroes- I assume the Dawn of Heroes and the Guilds were created in a latter time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Things change. Maybe the Begotten and the Rampant call a truce to deal with a particularly disruptive Hero and find some common ground. Beasts teach lesson through fear, lessons which do not necessarily oppose the philosophy of the Otodo. Some can easily support it. All it takes is one to take this thought to the family...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T00:41:48-07:00","id":560508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560506#post560506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Things change. Maybe the Begotten and the Rampant call a truce to deal with a particularly disruptive Hero and find some common ground. Beasts teach lesson through fear, lessons which do not necessarily oppose the philosophy of the Otodo. Some can easily support it. All it takes is one to take this thought to the family...</div> </div> </div> </div>I find myself agreeing with this. A whole lot can change in close to 400 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T01:10:17-07:00","id":560519,"title":"","content":"Huh, a sudden realization, also. 1640 would place the setting right smack in between the Shimabara Rebellion (1637-38) and the Keian Uprising (1651). The wheels turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T02:39:05-07:00","id":560573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560363#post560363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I'm still 50/50 on it. I prefer to have weaknesses inherit. And the cold iron weakness in Lost 1e is kind of lackluster, because it only applies to specific characters using specific powers, and even then, it only negates those advantages. To me, that's kinda boring as a weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hand-forged pure iron does aggravated to True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T03:05:21-07:00","id":560581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560573#post560573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hand-forged pure iron does aggravated to True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I'm thinking of upgrading the weakness on changelings as well.<br /> <br /> Particularly in the case of this being a Hunter book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T03:36:05-07:00","id":560608,"title":"","content":"You might want to change the name from Rampant to avoid confusion with the Merged Beasts. <br /> For Seitokuken, what counts as a &quot;demon&quot;? Inferno demons? D:tD demons? Beasts? Werewolves? Vampires? Sin-eaters? Prometheans?<br /> As someone said, Dorei-sei should be a standard resisted roll.<br /> How long does the ban from Kenshi last, or is it permanent?<br /> Devouring souls with Shinigami Buki seems too powerful for an Endowment. That's generally reserved for Rank 4+ angels or fifth level supernatural powers. Are the Soulless and Thrall Conditions permanent? Does it work on Beasts outside their Lair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T04:09:43-07:00","id":560616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560608#post560608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to change the name from Rampant to avoid confusion with the Merged Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. That's what they're called in the Beast book. So I don't want to cause dissonance there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560608#post560608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Seitokuken, what counts as a &quot;demon&quot;? Inferno demons? D:tD demons? Beasts? Werewolves? Vampires? Sin-eaters? Prometheans?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would take a ton of word count to draw distinctions on. Hunter deals with demons. Outside that, it's Storyteller fiat. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560608#post560608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone said, Dorei-sei should be a standard resisted roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't need to be seconded. I'll consider it in my pass. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560608#post560608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long does the ban from Kenshi last, or is it permanent?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking so. I might bother with a duration though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560608#post560608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Devouring souls with Shinigami Buki seems too powerful for an Endowment. That's generally reserved for Rank 4+ angels or fifth level supernatural powers. Are the Soulless and Thrall Conditions permanent? Does it work on Beasts outside their Lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Conditions are permanent until reversed. I'm sorry you feel it's too powerful. <br /> <br /> I don't know how those Conditions interact with Beasts. I don't know if they have any specific rules dealing with that, because the book isn't finished yet. I won't be addressing specific game line rules in a Hunter: The Vigil supplement, because down that path lies a word count rabbit hole and hours and hours of research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T04:43:01-07:00","id":560628,"title":"","content":"Read the Otodo in more detail now. My opinion asserts itself: it's a pretty cool write-up. Mechanical tinkering that might still need to be done to make one or two powers less wonky aside, I like the abilities and their descriptive flavor a lot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560363#post560363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I'm still 50/50 on it. I prefer to have weaknesses inherit. And the cold iron weakness in Lost 1e is kind of lackluster, because it only applies to specific characters using specific powers, and even then, it only negates those advantages. To me, that's kinda boring as a weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>It sorta doesn't do a lot as a weakness, no. I understand why you'd want to make it more interesting, but at the same time I do agree with the sentiment someone expressed that Changelings never felt like they needed a bane as significant as say, Silver for Werewolves.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's something that has to be considered in perspective of what it does to the True Fae and other beings from faerie like Hobgoblins and Huntsmen. It would be a little strange to me if cold iron (and its purer other, hand-forged iron) was more effective against changelings than the aforementioned fae denizens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:00:05-07:00","id":560647,"title":"","content":"Once again David, amazing work! You truly do spoil us with all of these awesome previews. Please don't ever stop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:31:25-07:00","id":560668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560628#post560628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sorta doesn't do a lot as a weakness, no. I understand why you'd want to make it more interesting, but at the same time I do agree with the sentiment someone expressed that Changelings never felt like they needed a bane as significant as say, Silver for Werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. For the sake of Changeling, it doesn't necessarily NEED one. But for Hunter, it adds something valuable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:36:46-07:00","id":560671,"title":"","content":"Ahhh, I get what you're saying. Yeah, that's a good point!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:39:16-07:00","id":560674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560616#post560616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>Originally posted by <b>Tau Neutrino</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560608#post560608\">View Post</a></i><br /> <i> Are the Soulless and Thrall Conditions permanent?</i><br /> Those Conditions are permanent until reversed. </div> </div> </div> </div>How can they be reversed? Is the soul not totally gone, or do they need a new one?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T05:44:38-07:00","id":560681,"title":"","content":"I have to admit. I was really liking it until I got to the abilities, and I read that first abilities and was about to say something aloud at my computer, but I turned the page and it settled everything. Really cool conspiracy you have there, and the powers are nicely unique and powerful without being overpowered, probably a good match for what the rest of second edition hunter will be like. Plus the whole tainted bloodline thing is a real nice idea to work off of.<br /> <br /> I particularly liked the Kenshi endowment, it's a nice flavorful ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:05:00-07:00","id":560715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560681#post560681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I particularly liked the Kenshi endowment, it's a nice flavorful ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>So did I; but I'm liable to let the Rampant &amp; the 7th Generation learn each other's powers AFTER they meet and teach each other. It is basically Castigation anyway; their cultural bias led to the difference in abilities. This doesn't mean you can cherry pick; somehow I don't think the Otodo &amp; the Lucifuge get along so well. Their relationship seems more like it would be a truce than a union.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:31:52-07:00","id":560728,"title":"","content":"Now I'm left wondering how the Otodo see the Inferno.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:35:36-07:00","id":560730,"title":"","content":"I can't imagine the two groups sharing their powers under most circumstances. <br /> <br /> Both groups police their own even unto death, feeling that kind of responsibility I can't imagine they'd be too keen on sharing their powers- Sharing powers would make them share responsibility if the student then falls, and I can't see either group willing to let an outsider, distant cousin or not, police them.<br /> <br /> Secondly, I can't imagine the scions of hell being too trusting- Why would the Otodo trust that the Lady of Milan has no secret agenda when the Lucifuge suspect her? How could they be sure that a castigation ritual isn't slowly corruptive or gives the Lady some power over them? Or vice versa- The Lucifuge doesn't trust their own leadership, why would they trust the Otodo's leadership?<br /> <br /> And would the Lucifuge herself be happy to have a member giving away trade secrets? It's not like the lucifuge are under the mistaken impression that the Lady wouldn't have them killed, I can't imagine the leaders of the otodo are that different.<br /> <br /> Of course, this also all presupposes that the otodo and the lucifuge even acknowledge a common heritage. Oni equals demon? In character, they might not jump to that conclusion, and how could they prove it in character? I don't see a DNA test of all the otodo and all the lucifuge to discover common ancestors anytime soon.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T06:51:22-07:00","id":560776,"title":"","content":"The Lucifuge has a &quot;recruit or befriend monsters that aren't completely evil&quot; outlook. I really doubt that they'll be opponents in any sense. At worst, they'll be indifferent. Oh, they likely won't merge as groups, but becoming allies? Very likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:41:31-07:00","id":561057,"title":"","content":"I've posted before about the idea of having local twists on existing groups, but you've really outdone yourself with this; you managed to make what I would've seen as a thoroughly Christian organization fit into Japanese myth like it ain't no thing.<br /> <br /> The new powers are great, although I'm a little iffy on Kigo having an indefinite duration and I have to echo the sentiment that inflicting Soulless/Thrall is beyond the power scale of Hunters, especially given how hard that is to inflict even with a moderately powerful Mage. I think Willpower drain with Shinigami Buki is powerful enough without those Conditions, given how Dread Powers are fueled by Willpower. I'm also surprised that devouring a soul isn't considered a Breaking Point; that's pretty evil, even if you're doing it to a monster.<br /> <br /> Kenshi and Kaibutsu are both really the kind of powers that I read and immediately need to build a character around.<br /> <br /> Dorei-sei is written a little strangely, setting the target number of successes equal to Seitokuken dots, rather than 3/5 successes or a contested roll. The same mechanic shows up in Kaibutsu as well, and feels a little wonky.<br /> <br /> I can't wait to see the other groups; the Ama-san immediately catch my eye, but the Gimu and Hotogisu are both interesting as well. I'm sure the Bijin will make me cry, just the same as the 2e Daeva and probably the 2e Galateids as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:43:03-07:00","id":561059,"title":"","content":"Make you cry how, exactly?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T12:49:08-07:00","id":561061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560728#post560728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm left wondering how the Otodo see the Inferno.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shinto, due to Japan's cultural squeamishness with the dead and the disease necrotized tissue carries, has a concept of evil being a disease. That's why you see the idea of people being corrupted by dark knowledge or malign power in anime a lot, to the Japanese mindset, their recklessness with handling the metaphorical body meant they came down with a bad case of Megalomanitis. That and the idea of selfishness inherently corrupting any goal.<br /> <br /> I imagine they <i>began </i>with the idea that Infernal demons are corrupted versions of other beings, and that discovering the Inferno is an actual dimension of its own motivated by hunger for darker passions would actually solve more of their questions than raise them. From there Buddhism would probably fill in the rest of the gaps, true Dominions being the inhabitants/prisoners of Jigoku (aka Naraka, with a Japanese name and ruler).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:13:53-07:00","id":561072,"title":"","content":"I like them a lot. I did notice that they don't have the traditional three subgroups. Is there a reason for that?<br /> <br /> One small change that I'd love to see is if your first dot of Seitokuken automatically gave you Unseen Sense (Demons), or Unseen Sense (Oni) - same difference - in addition to the universal sense they get later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-19-2015, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:31:03-07:00","id":561095,"title":"","content":"What do we know about the modern Hotogisu? Are they definitely a Hunter Compact/Conspiracy we may see in the 2nd Edition HtV book (assuming it happens)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:34:03-07:00","id":561120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561095#post561095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do we know about the modern Hotogisu? Are they definitely a Hunter Compact/Conspiracy we may see in the 2nd Edition HtV book (assuming it happens)?</div> </div> </div> </div>They got a Mystery Cult Initiation in VtR 2e that gave them some minor powers and junk?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T13:58:21-07:00","id":561161,"title":"","content":"They also seem to show up in every Tokyo entry in 2nd edition- they have strong ties to Vampires, but they seem to have connections with supernaturals all around Tokyo. In Vampire, they are described as the &quot;fourth great power&quot; in Tokyo's hidden world, and they have some sort of 5 years plan to dominance, which has started at 2010. They also research all kinds of occult techniques of other supers and they try to copy and recreate them.<br /> <br /> Now all we have to do is wait for people to scream &quot;metaplot!&quot; every time they are mentioned, and we can call them the new God Machine and wait for Hunter's Hototogisu Chronicle book :P<br /> <br /> (it is a joke, please don't kill me)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:05:03-07:00","id":561188,"title":"","content":"Also, I have to mention that I have no problem with Shinigami Buki and giving Hunters the ability to force the Soulless/ Thrall Conditions. On the other hand, some of the groups I wrote do things like using Covers, using magical Practices, buying Host Aspects, creating Old Laws and making Angels out of their souls out of the opinion that hunters should do things that would make supers say &quot;WTF?!&quot;, that mechanics should support the fluff at all cause and that Game Balance is a myth, so I may not be the best example :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:42:33-07:00","id":561221,"title":"","content":"I'm leaning toward the idea at my own table that the Otodo is modern day have been nominally assimilated as one of the diverse &quot;Families&quot; that make up the Lucifuge - but everyone knows they don't listen to Milan and run their own affairs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T18:44:08-07:00","id":561466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561072#post561072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like them a lot. I did notice that they don't have the traditional three subgroups. Is there a reason for that?<br /> <br /> One small change that I'd love to see is if your first dot of Seitokuken automatically gave you Unseen Sense (Demons), or Unseen Sense (Oni) - same difference - in addition to the universal sense they get later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Long story short: I totally forgot. <br /> <br /> I'll add the single-function Unseen Sense at the first dot. I'll probably specify oni, as opposed to the broader demons, because I don't want to take away from the value of their sight power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T18:45:39-07:00","id":561467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561095#post561095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do we know about the modern Hotogisu? Are they definitely a Hunter Compact/Conspiracy we may see in the 2nd Edition HtV book (assuming it happens)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so. Maybe? Not sure. Depends on who ends up developing the Hunter Second Edition book, honestly. They're not properly just a Conspiracy anymore. They're a lot of things. A Cryptopoly, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T18:47:25-07:00","id":561469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561161#post561161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also seem to show up in every Tokyo entry in 2nd edition- they have strong ties to Vampires, but they seem to have connections with supernaturals all around Tokyo. In Vampire, they are described as the &quot;fourth great power&quot; in Tokyo's hidden world, and they have some sort of 5 years plan to dominance, which has started at 2010. They also research all kinds of occult techniques of other supers and they try to copy and recreate them.<br /> <br /> Now all we have to do is wait for people to scream &quot;metaplot!&quot; every time they are mentioned, and we can call them the new God Machine and wait for Hunter's Hototogisu Chronicle book :P<br /> <br /> (it is a joke, please don't kill me)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's kind of a metaplot. Tokyo's an exercise in how you can do metaplots within the framework of the NWoD, without making the whole game line about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T19:15:26-07:00","id":561507,"title":"","content":"Could you clarify how the Kenshi power works? Especially this line: <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your character\u2019s Seitokuken dots act as the monster\u2019s spirit Rank for the purpose of determining the ban level.</span></span><br /> <br /> I don't understand it. What is meant with ban level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T19:19:31-07:00","id":561508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561507#post561507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you clarify how the Kenshi power works? Especially this line:<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Your character\u2019s Seitokuken dots act as the monster\u2019s spirit Rank for the purpose of determining the ban level.</span></span><br /> <br /> I don't understand it. What is meant with ban level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits of different Ranks have different types of Bans. Higher level spirits have more potent Bans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T23:04:40-07:00","id":561612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561466#post561466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll add the single-function Unseen Sense at the first dot. I'll probably specify oni, as opposed to the broader demons, because I don't want to take away from the value of their sight power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T04:37:02-07:00","id":561778,"title":"","content":"So I assume all the Dark Eras chapters will be as proper 2nd Editions? Becuase here are Hunter rules using GMC base, with Integrity in place of Morality...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T04:47:57-07:00","id":561788,"title":"","content":"...I would not count on it. I do think that those games that currently have or having a 2nd edition being written will be more than likely.<br /> I would not expect GMC equivalent (ala Mortal Remains) for the games that do not have 2nd editions in development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T06:37:42-07:00","id":561839,"title":"","content":"I suppose I should say these things here.<br /> <br /> \u2726 Why are they called Rampant/Otodo? They actually come off as rather calm in this write up.<br /> \u2726 Why do they take the same path as the Lucifuge? There's not really any reason given for why they turn into monster hunters instead of just using their ogreblood to wreck shit. It just goes right from &quot;they were the children of a fishing village that mated with oni&quot; to &quot;they fight their dark heritage&quot;. <br /> \u2726 I'm not sure if you just messed up the formatting or what, but the sidebar flows right back into The Enemy on Beasts and Heroes.<br /> \u2726 Aren't there several Japanese myths of non-evil oni? You don't get the cool clubs, but why go oni? Why not just yokai? That's about as generic as &quot;demon&quot; anyway. Or Akuma.<br /> \u2726 Is it a new thing that Iron does Aggravated to Changelings? It typically just cuts through Contracts, but otherwise does no increased damage.<br /> \u2726 How do the Otodo keep track of genealogical records? They're constantly traveling, but able to keep tabs on when someone they knocked up gets pregnant in a preindustrial society?<br /> \u2726 Why do they even travel the Lonesome Road in the first place? One sample Hunter is someone born a &quot;legacy Hunter&quot;, but elsewhere we're told that they're rare and solitary. How do they keep extensive notes on who they've slept with when they're also travelers? Are they carrying around huge &quot;little black books&quot;? The &quot;keeping the lineage&quot; aspect is neat, but it doesn't really feel like it's handled well. Wouldn't it be better for them to operate out of a central compound or something like that and take on wives or husbands? Those non-blood members of the clan could even provide support and aid. <br /> \u2726 Why do they not work together more than a single hunt? For what reason do they feel that it's better to go alone? The Lucifuge are a modern group spread out across the entire world and there are only six-hundred sixty-six of them to deal with an untold number of demons and L'Enfant Terrible; why does a small family of ogreblooded stay away from each other instead of working together?<br /> \u2726 Why are the Malleus Maleficarum a power in Japan during an era after the Christians were massacred? Why would they be a power at all? It doesn't make sense to include them when there are so many better Westerrn Conspiracies to involve; the Acheron Shipping &amp; Trading Company, for instance. Even working in the first contact between the Lucifuge and Otodo would be interesting. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yasuke\" target=\"_blank\">Yasuke the Black Samurai</a> bringing the Ascending Ones to Japan would be more reasonable.<br /> <br /> Now for the powers. I realize that you're not fond of &quot;white room combat&quot;, but a lot of these really don't feel very thought out. I'm going to try to break down as well as I can why; I might even do a playtest of them, though, because issues aside it still sounds like stupid fun to play demon ninjas in Hunter.<br /> <b>\u2726 Seitokuken </b>Why are their powers gained so differently than the Lucifuge? They don't need to work for it, they just wait six hours and take 2L, which is a pretty steep penalty considering that's going to stick around for four days. Hunters who are out of commission for four days are not very useful Hunters. The burned veins is neat, though. <br /> \u2726 Does Seitokuken not threaten Integrity directly the way that failed Castigation powers do? &quot;They might be a Breaking Point&quot; without listing which ones would be a Breaking Point is also kind of half-assing it. Does Kaibutsu cause a Breaking Point (In either the Otodo or onlookers)? Is Shinigami Buki worse than stabbing someone? Saying that without elaborating on it is unhelpful and gives no real guidance. You've said &quot;I think you should do something a particular way, but I won't say what that way is&quot;.<br /> <b>\u2726</b> <b>Dorei-Sei</b> is unfun. It doesn't really make for an interesting game if a character can face off against the demon they've been tracking and say &quot;Kill yourself&quot;. It's anticlimactic and so powerful that it invalidates every other ability. The other Birthrights exist as back up if your Integrity is too low to make a command or if you fight something that isn't ephemeral. The fact that Integrity of PCs tends to be in the 4-6 range is the only real downside. Does using it against Spirits count as a Breaking Point? What about Thralls? It's also an incredibly wonky ability; you roll to activate it and as long as you get one success they're commanded unless they can Contest against your dots in Seitokuken.<br /> <b>\u2726 Hannya</b> feels like it would be better off as full Aura Perception 2e style (like Auspex's) as opposed to what it is. It actually seems kind of weak.<br /> <b>\u2726 Kaibutsu </b>is at once devastatingly powerful and incredibly underwhelming. You turn into a giant oni. You get +2 Size and Health. You get 2/1 armour. Your hands and teeth are lethal weapons. You can add between \u25cf and \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf dots to your physical attributes. You can--rather expensively--heal damage. But also all of your clothes are destroyed and you freak out mortals and show yourself to be a monster. Unfortunately monsters are unlikely to wait for you to spend several turns powering up. Even a character with high Integrity is likely to take at least two turns Hulking out.<br /> <b>\u2726 Kenshi</b> as written does not make any sense. I'm not sure what it means by &quot;seitokuken dots act as the monster's spirit Rank for the purpose of determining the ban level&quot;. That seems like characters with <i>less</i> Birthright are better at Kenshi. I also think that this power should refer to <i>banes</i>; Bans are mystical compulsions, while banes are the thing you smack them with until they die.<br /> <b>\u2726 Kigo </b>is another of those needlessly powerful powers. The damage being half-Birthright seems a bit much, and it feels like you <i>intend</i> for it to involve a touch attack. It does a ludicrous amount of damage to vampires and the undead, to the point that it's better to slap fight them until they're covered in \u3060\u307e\u308c. Assuming they don't die before the third hiragana. The ability to track seems more useful when used to mark allies than it does with the Undead, but there it is. <br /> <b>\u2726 Shinigami Buki</b> This power is also quite unusual. You roll once and then mechanically you do nothing for the next X+Y turns where X is your successes and Y is your Birthright. Presumably the demon will be trying to escape at this point. Is this an Instant action, or is it Reflexive each turn? Why bother even rolling, why not just &quot;as a Reflexive action spend a point of Willpower and over a number of turns equal to Seitokuken the victim loses one Willpower per turn, and ephemeral beings take 1 lethal damage&quot;? Then it would be more explicit that you can devote your actions proper to grappling.<br /> <b>\u2726 Shonetsu Jogoku </b>is another of those ridiculously strong powers. A four damage weapon is nothing to sneeze at, though for most characters that's not even going to be as good as the weapon they all carry. The range is also so short that it might as well not even be a thrown weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T06:58:24-07:00","id":561863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I should say these things here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least you're consistent between forums.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T07:01:13-07:00","id":561866,"title":"","content":"I meant I should say it here as opposed to the Blog; are you implying I should be <i>in</i>consistent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T09:19:45-07:00","id":562000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose I should say these things here.<br /> <br /> \u2726 Why are they called Rampant/Otodo? They actually come off as rather calm in this write up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they've got demons inside them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2726 Why do they take the same path as the Lucifuge? There's not really any reason given for why they turn into monster hunters instead of just using their ogreblood to wreck shit. It just goes right from &quot;they were the children of a fishing village that mated with oni&quot; to &quot;they fight their dark heritage&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may flesh that out a bit. I think it's perfectly reasonable to leave that to discern in your stories. They're not the only ones; this writeup is specifically focusing on the ones who take up the Vigil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2726 I'm not sure if you just messed up the formatting or what, but the sidebar flows right back into The Enemy on Beasts and Heroes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidebars just go wherever in our documents. The layout person puts them on the page we tell them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2726 Aren't there several Japanese myths of non-evil oni? You don't get the cool clubs, but why go oni? Why not just yokai? That's about as generic as &quot;demon&quot; anyway. Or Akuma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there are knon-evil oni. The reason is, because of the parallel to the Lucifuge. I thought that was pretty obvious. Most stories about akuma have them too volatile to deal with humans. I discussed this all with a friend who is deeply versed in folklore. I told her the story of the Lucifuge. I asked about a few things, akuma included. She told me it wouldn't work, and that she's read stories of oni and human couplings, that oni would fit best in the role.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2726 Is it a new thing that Iron does Aggravated to Changelings? It typically just cuts through Contracts, but otherwise does no increased damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has already been brought up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2726 How do the Otodo keep track of genealogical records? They're constantly traveling, but able to keep tabs on when someone they knocked up gets pregnant in a preindustrial society?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was inferred that their connections/note sharing would allow them to network sufficiently to keep tabs on people here and there. Just because they're always traveling, doesn't mean they never go to the same place twice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2726 Why do they even travel the Lonesome Road in the first place? One sample Hunter is someone born a &quot;legacy Hunter&quot;, but elsewhere we're told that they're rare and solitary. How do they keep extensive notes on who they've slept with when they're also travelers? Are they carrying around huge &quot;little black books&quot;? The &quot;keeping the lineage&quot; aspect is neat, but it doesn't really feel like it's handled well. Wouldn't it be better for them to operate out of a central compound or something like that and take on wives or husbands? Those non-blood members of the clan could even provide support and aid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. Maybe? I don't think it's objectively any better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2726 Why do they not work together more than a single hunt? For what reason do they feel that it's better to go alone? The Lucifuge are a modern group spread out across the entire world and there are only six-hundred sixty-six of them to deal with an untold number of demons and L'Enfant Terrible; why does a small family of ogreblooded stay away from each other instead of working together?</div> </div> </div> </div>Coverage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2726 Why are the Malleus Maleficarum a power in Japan during an era after the Christians were massacred? Why would they be a power at all? It doesn't make sense to include them when there are so many better Westerrn Conspiracies to involve; the Acheron Shipping &amp; Trading Company, for instance. Even working in the first contact between the Lucifuge and Otodo would be interesting. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yasuke\" target=\"_blank\">Yasuke the Black Samurai</a> bringing the Ascending Ones to Japan would be more reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Malleus are not a power. A few of them exist. They've made sufficiently bad impressions that a group of traveling hunters is aware of them. They came over with the Dutch. Others are involved; it just turns out that the demon-blooded group has an opinion on a group of outsiders that came in to hunt demons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now for the powers. I realize that you're not fond of &quot;white room combat&quot;, but a lot of these really don't feel very thought out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry. I should have made this clear: This is a first draft, not a second, not a final.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u2726 Seitokuken </b>Why are their powers gained so differently than the Lucifuge? They don't need to work for it, they just wait six hours and take 2L, which is a pretty steep penalty considering that's going to stick around for four days. Hunters who are out of commission for four days are not very useful Hunters. The burned veins is neat, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Switching out rites requires a rededication of the character\u2019s energy, though, and that takes time. The player rolls Resolve + Occult as an extended action. The target number of successes is 20 minus character\u2019s rating in Endowments (Castigation), and the player makes one roll per day in which the character spends at least four hours studying, fasting, flagellating or otherwise preparing himself for the change. As the total number of successes climbs, the character suffers nightmares, sweats, spontaneous nosebleeds and other ailments, and then finally peace as the change sets in.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lucifuge have a hell of a time. It isn't reflected as actual damage, but we're talking about an average of about 10 days of trauma. Flagellation is not easy. You're assuming that two lethal damage puts the character completely out of commission. I don't know about your games, but in my games, characters with 2-4 levels of damage do all sorts of shit. They have to; there's often something at stake that can't wait. Like Patrick Swayze said, &quot;Pain don't hurt&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2726 Does Seitokuken not threaten Integrity directly the way that failed Castigation powers do? &quot;They might be a Breaking Point&quot; without listing which ones would be a Breaking Point is also kind of half-assing it. Does Kaibutsu cause a Breaking Point (In either the Otodo or onlookers)? Is Shinigami Buki worse than stabbing someone? Saying that without elaborating on it is unhelpful and gives no real guidance. You've said &quot;I think you should do something a particular way, but I won't say what that way is&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It means the Integrity rules aren't so cut and dry as the Morality rules, and some characters suffer breaking points for different things than others. Sorry if you feel that's half-assing it. Well, not sorry. But, you have your opinions, which trend in a very specific, very consistent direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u2726</b> <b>Dorei-Sei</b> is unfun. It doesn't really make for an interesting game if a character can face off against the demon they've been tracking and say &quot;Kill yourself&quot;. It's anticlimactic and so powerful that it invalidates every other ability. The other Birthrights exist as back up if your Integrity is too low to make a command or if you fight something that isn't ephemeral. The fact that Integrity of PCs tends to be in the 4-6 range is the only real downside. Does using it against Spirits count as a Breaking Point? What about Thralls? It's also an incredibly wonky ability; you roll to activate it and as long as you get one success they're commanded unless they can Contest against your dots in Seitokuken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. I will probably tone it down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u2726 Hannya</b> feels like it would be better off as full Aura Perception 2e style (like Auspex's) as opposed to what it is. It actually seems kind of weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a thought. I might do that. Although I really prefer the passive element here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u2726 Kaibutsu </b>is at once devastatingly powerful and incredibly underwhelming. You turn into a giant oni. You get +2 Size and Health. You get 2/1 armour. Your hands and teeth are lethal weapons. You can add between \u25cf and \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf dots to your physical attributes. You can--rather expensively--heal damage. But also all of your clothes are destroyed and you freak out mortals and show yourself to be a monster. Unfortunately monsters are unlikely to wait for you to spend several turns powering up. Even a character with high Integrity is likely to take at least two turns Hulking out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm mulling over that. Maybe making it require 3 successes. I'm hesitant to make it instant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u2726 Kenshi</b> as written does not make any sense. I'm not sure what it means by &quot;seitokuken dots act as the monster's spirit Rank for the purpose of determining the ban level&quot;. That seems like characters with <i>less</i> Birthright are better at Kenshi. I also think that this power should refer to <i>banes</i>; Bans are mystical compulsions, while banes are the thing you smack them with until they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It means bans. You literally place a ban on something. It cannot do X. The higher its rank, the more prohibitive that can be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u2726 Kigo </b>is another of those needlessly powerful powers. The damage being half-Birthright seems a bit much, and it feels like you <i>intend</i> for it to involve a touch attack. It does a ludicrous amount of damage to vampires and the undead, to the point that it's better to slap fight them until they're covered in \u3060\u307e\u308c. Assuming they don't die before the third hiragana. The ability to track seems more useful when used to mark allies than it does with the Undead, but there it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I also tend to draft higher, and whittle down from there. This one will likely get toned down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u2726 Shinigami Buki</b> This power is also quite unusual. You roll once and then mechanically you do nothing for the next X+Y turns where X is your successes and Y is your Birthright. Presumably the demon will be trying to escape at this point. Is this an Instant action, or is it Reflexive each turn? Why bother even rolling, why not just &quot;as a Reflexive action spend a point of Willpower and over a number of turns equal to Seitokuken the victim loses one Willpower per turn, and ephemeral beings take 1 lethal damage&quot;? Then it would be more explicit that you can devote your actions proper to grappling.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually like the turns/Seitokuken.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561839#post561839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u2726 Shonetsu Jogoku </b>is another of those ridiculously strong powers. A four damage weapon is nothing to sneeze at, though for most characters that's not even going to be as good as the weapon they all carry. The range is also so short that it might as well not even be a thrown weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll up the range a bit. I don't want to make it too far though. I don't think a 4-damage weapon is inherently broken, particularly since it costs Merit points and Willpower. As opposed to a mundane 4-damage weapon, which doesn't take those things. I initially considered making it half dots, rounded down. But I debated over that, since at its very peak level, it'd be less effective than some mundane weapons. That's anticlimactic for something that necessitates your being part monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 06-20-2015, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T09:39:37-07:00","id":562009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=561866#post561866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant I should say it here as opposed to the Blog; are you implying I should be <i>in</i>consistent?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I'm implying that you've been generally negative on just about everything Onyx Path and/or White Wolf, regardless of the forum. The most positive post I've seen from you was about Geist, which in your opinion, has a 'ton of problems that you've decided to fix out of the goodness of your heart.'<br /> <br /> It's fine. And I really couldn't care less. Just pointing out something I've noticed about you as a poster. Very critical and very negative.<br /> <br /> All the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T09:47:15-07:00","id":562013,"title":"","content":"OTOH if there's a time and place to post criticisms/concerns it'd be an Open Dev thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T10:10:27-07:00","id":562060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562013#post562013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OTOH if there's a time and place to post criticisms/concerns it'd be an Open Dev thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly the case. But that said, I kind of feel Dude's point. There's a certain point where it's hard to listen to long, constant criticism from someone because it seems they're just never going to be on board with anything you're doing. I can totally get behind participating in the discussion; I post these things here so there can be conversation. But there's a point right around the time he's bringing up that he knows multiple people who apparently want to hit me over my work in a roleplaying game, I just wonder if maybe we're not going to see eye to eye. <br /> <br /> Most of the stuff in that particular comment seemed relatively good faith. So, I'll take it to heart and consider it when doing my revisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T10:32:46-07:00","id":562076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562060#post562060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Yes, there are knon-evil oni. The reason is, because of the parallel to the Lucifuge. I thought that was pretty obvious. Most stories about akuma have them too volatile to deal with humans. I discussed this all with a friend who is deeply versed in folklore. I told her the story of the Lucifuge. I asked about a few things, akuma included. She told me it wouldn't work, and that she's read stories of oni and human couplings, that oni would fit best in the role.</span></span></span>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, now I'm curious to look up the differences between oni and akuma.<br /> <br /> EDIT - from what little I've seen, akuma is roughly equivalent to &quot;An evil spirit envisioned as a flying monster with fiery head and eyes, often with a sword.&quot; Sounds very Fallen-Angel-like. I wonder if it akuma legends would be appropriate for Demon: the Descent. Being too volatile for humans also works into that angle a bit - when you see their Demon Form, you're not in a good place. That said, I haven't really found any good, in depth description, so I'm kinda stretching here now. Moving on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-20-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T10:53:51-07:00","id":562084,"title":"","content":"Don't quote me on this, but far as I know akuma have much more universally malevolent connotations in their interactions with humans than oni. The latter are also wicked but they're in a way closer to humans and not seen inherently as evil as the former.<br /> <br /> That's about the extent of my knowledge on it though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T11:10:24-07:00","id":562093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562084#post562084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't quote me on this, but far as I know akuma have much more universally malevolent connotations in their interactions with humans than oni. The latter are also wicked but they're in a way closer to humans and not seen inherently as evil as the former.<br /> <br /> That's about the extent of my knowledge on it though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, that's the impression I got as well. But then, the same universal-evil connotations is traditionally true of fallen angels in christian lore, which is why I'm wondering if there's parallels involved. In Hunter terms, the oni would would be lesser demons, the akuma the greter demons, and tennin the institutional demons?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, this is off topic. I am really liking the Otodo as presented, I am just a bit eager to look into how Tokyo would present their version of the Otodo's oni in the game. Its a curious subject for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-20-2015, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:18:54-07:00","id":562174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562060#post562060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's certainly the case. But that said, I kind of feel Dude's point. There's a certain point where it's hard to listen to long, constant criticism from someone because it seems they're just never going to be on board with anything you're doing. I can totally get behind participating in the discussion; I post these things here so there can be conversation. But there's a point right around the time he's bringing up that he knows multiple people who apparently want to hit me over my work in a roleplaying game, I just wonder if maybe we're not going to see eye to eye.<br /> <br /> Most of the stuff in that particular comment seemed relatively good faith. So, I'll take it to heart and consider it when doing my revisions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have taken the expletive filled anger from both Japanese posters on 4chan and a Japanese-American friend who has since fallen off the internet, removed the swearing, and brought those concerns to you. You <i>cannot</i> be so insulated from criticism that you don't realize that there are Japanese people who feel you exemplify a typical ex pat that wants to make Japan like America. I know you can't be, because I've seen people telling you that. You asked for comments and criticism. In another thread, you said that only 5% of playtesters ever give feedback beyond &quot;seems good&quot;. I spent two or three hours reading over and dissecting what you wrote, noting both narrative and mechanical concerns in very detailed way. I don't appreciate the insinuation that my doing so may or may not be in what you consider &quot;good faith&quot;.<br /> The other day Chris Allen deconstructed some fan work I wrote. He tore that mess <i>up</i> like a pack of ravens descending on a dying cat. His list of criticisms was longer than what I actually wrote. I didn't dismiss them, or question whether or not they came in good faith. Hell, I think I've got a little crush on him after that. Dave wades into the 4chan threads and he's a damned <i>rockstar</i>. Not ten hours ago I ranted to him about how it was hard not to idolize Rose. Even in the other thread where you and Dude of Legend feel that I'm &quot;just never going to be on board with anything&quot;, I was expressing excitement over the potential of Beast, hopefulness over what it might look like in the future, and I think like four times pointed out Humanity/Touchstones as amazing game design. I have <i>major</i> problems with you from several of our past interactions across the internet, and I've <i>still</i> been as polite with you as I can. And, yes, I know several people who &quot;apparently want to hit you over your game design&quot; because the internet beyond these forums is an open and free place where people can talk about many things and use angry rhetoric. I even <i>still</i> told the guy he should email you even though he hates you and thinks it won't change anything. I have even defended you for things that I feel either aren't your fault or aren't problems.<br /> <br /> I have been <i>exceedingly</i> good faith, and I would appreciate that operated in the same capacity without making implications about my motives. I'm sorry if you feel that my in depth critique that you, you know, asked for is somehow mean or rude. I'm trying to take an active hand in critiquing a game <i>that I like</i> because some of the developers have expressed a disappointment in the quality of feedback beyond &quot;seems good&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dude of Legend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562009#post562009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I'm implying that you've been generally negative on just about everything Onyx Path and/or White Wolf, regardless of the forum. The most positive post I've seen from you was about Geist, which in your opinion, has a 'ton of problems that you've decided to fix out of the goodness of your heart.'</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware that I needed to take an oath of fealty to never express a negative opinion. Here I was under the impression that critical deconstruction of something was the hallmark of being a fan. Although I'm surprised at how you can say the only thing nice I've had to say is about Geist. I was under the impression that I've brought up Humanity/Touchstones enough that it was getting old, because, frankly, I love them and think they're brilliant at subtly hammering home the theme of Vampire through ludology.<br /> <br /> If you need more things I like, I actually really love what Hill himself has done with Bloodlines; they were previously one of the only things I liked about Vampire--and something I wish other games did just as well--and I think the 2e ones are phenomenal, not necessarily in the Bloodlines themselves but in how they redefine how a Bloodline works. And, again, I <i>love</i> Bloodlines compared to Lodges, Legacies, Entitlements, and so forth. I think there are some mechanical issues with them, but criticizing something doesn't mean someone hates it. Often the opposite, I find.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-20-2015, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:49:50-07:00","id":562181,"title":"","content":"Also, I think Kenshi needs to be elaborated on, if that's the case, because the impression I got from references to talisman was that you're making a beat stick as opposed to forcing &quot;you must stand still&quot; on a demon; I suppose that means that the Birthright rank means you get more detailed restrictions, which does make sense (since you're able to customize it). Would someone be able to use a ban at a lower level (&quot;stay within this circle&quot; instead of &quot;explode when I look at you&quot;), in case they wanted to capture a yokai (&quot;where are you keeping them, monster?&quot;) It's actually a neat system. (Hey, look, explicit praise).<br /> I also suppose I should have removed the &quot;ridiculously strong&quot; bit about Shonetsu Jogoku, because on further reading it feels strong, but weaker than what a real weapon would do. Good for a last resort weapon, but not as a primary means of defense. Then again, it's also a weapon that doesn't penalize defense or anything like that.<br /> For Kaibutsu, why not just make it a flat turn of transformation where you can do nothing but use Defense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:57:07-07:00","id":562187,"title":"","content":"ammm so this looks kinda personal and all, so maybe the safe thing to do would be that everyone would just calm down? So lets not go and blame each other for things like bringing negativity for threads or making long speeches about how hurt we are. This is a nice thread, and I don't want to see it ruined..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T14:02:36-07:00","id":562192,"title":"","content":"If you've got personal issues from the dark corners of the internet, maybe that's something to talk about in private rather than bringing it into this discussion.<br /> <br /> I think your suggestion for Kaibutsu, of making it an instant action is a good one that still makes it significant while also allowing for quicker transformations. Transforming powers in these games, if they're not like, a total metamorphosis that doesn't change, generally feel like they should be instant or reflexive, as it keeps them exciting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T14:27:54-07:00","id":562229,"title":"","content":"MUSHes are bad, but I mean, I wouldn't call them the dark corner of the internet. I dropped it like a bad habit ages ago, but I even hear WanWic is back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 06-20-2015, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T18:26:04-07:00","id":562441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562181#post562181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think Kenshi needs to be elaborated on, if that's the case, because the impression I got from references to talisman was that you're making a beat stick as opposed to forcing &quot;you must stand still&quot; on a demon; I suppose that means that the Birthright rank means you get more detailed restrictions, which does make sense (since you're able to customize it). Would someone be able to use a ban at a lower level (&quot;stay within this circle&quot; instead of &quot;explode when I look at you&quot;), in case they wanted to capture a yokai (&quot;where are you keeping them, monster?&quot;) It's actually a neat system. (Hey, look, explicit praise).<br /> I also suppose I should have removed the &quot;ridiculously strong&quot; bit about Shonetsu Jogoku, because on further reading it feels strong, but weaker than what a real weapon would do. Good for a last resort weapon, but not as a primary means of defense. Then again, it's also a weapon that doesn't penalize defense or anything like that.<br /> For Kaibutsu, why not just make it a flat turn of transformation where you can do nothing but use Defense?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll clarify. But the primary intention would be to get them to stand still, or to otherwise restrain them (physically or in a more abstract sense). You could use it to make weapons or whatever? And yeah, you can use it at lower level. <br /> <br /> I'll give it a few tries with the Shonetsu Jogoku. <br /> <br /> Does anyone else have any input on Kaibutsu? I don't mind that change. Full turn but not denying Defense isn't a bad idea. (Although there's a sick part of me that wants to deny Defense as a funny way to poke fun at transformation sequences.) <br /> <br /> And sorry if that came across as particularly harsh. I actually meant it relatively positive; it seemed you weren't trying to be particularly negative here. I don't know about other forums. The few times I've waded into 4chan's gaming stuff, I saw people discussing my sexuality and misrepresenting it as a way to dismiss straw opinions they think I have. So, I avoid it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T18:27:28-07:00","id":562444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562174#post562174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In another thread, you said that only 5% of playtesters ever give feedback beyond &quot;seems good&quot;. I spent two or three hours reading over and dissecting what you wrote, noting both narrative and mechanical concerns in very detailed way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er. I want to say, I appreciate your notes. <br /> <br /> I don't count you among that 5%, because (and correct me if I'm wrong) you're just commenting on the stuff, not actually play testing. Am I wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T18:32:59-07:00","id":562448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562229#post562229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MUSHes are bad, but I mean, I wouldn't call them the dark corner of the internet. I dropped it like a bad habit ages ago, but I even hear WanWic is back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I find online games really useful for things like play testing. I play tested a lot of 2e's core rules on it, and that actually helped a lot with seeing how they flowed. On big projects, I tend to look for a chat or other large-scale online player to consult, because their experience is unique, and can speak to trends in player choices that go way beyond a few small tables.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T19:41:12-07:00","id":562514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562444#post562444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er. I want to say, I appreciate your notes.<br /> <br /> I don't count you among that 5%, because (and correct me if I'm wrong) you're just commenting on the stuff, not actually play testing. Am I wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't, but I'm thinking about running a one shot. I do like the concept. And I really am only being critical because I like WoD. I also apologize if as Dude of Legend feels I come off as only being negative.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562448#post562448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I find online games really useful for things like play testing. I play tested a lot of 2e's core rules on it, and that actually helped a lot with seeing how they flowed. On big projects, I tend to look for a chat or other large-scale online player to consult, because their experience is unique, and can speak to trends in player choices that go way beyond a few small tables.</div> </div> </div> </div>I lost faith in MUSHes about when an ST's Mage skin burned down my Sanctum, deleted his character to avoid consequences, and then resanctioned a character in a venue he wasn't ST of. The whole freeform MMO thing'd be great if only it wasn't full of people who either want to PVP or create cliques that rule the venue in and out of setting. Plus there's never enough STs so there's never any real consequences. After WanWic I decided I'd stick to IRC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T20:39:42-07:00","id":562549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562514#post562514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I lost faith in MUSHes about when an ST's Mage skin burned down my Sanctum, deleted his character to avoid consequences, and then resanctioned a character in a venue he wasn't ST of. The whole freeform MMO thing'd be great if only it wasn't full of people who either want to PVP or create cliques that rule the venue in and out of setting. Plus there's never enough STs so there's never any real consequences. After WanWic I decided I'd stick to IRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel you. There's a ton of shit. But, there's also a value for my work. I haven't touched one in a couple years now. Just too much toxicity and nonsense competition, not enough focus on making stories meaningful and interesting. But I keep thinking I might try to do one again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T01:32:22-07:00","id":562742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=560506#post560506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Things change. Maybe the Begotten and the Rampant call a truce to deal with a particularly disruptive Hero and find some common ground. Beasts teach lesson through fear, lessons which do not necessarily oppose the philosophy of the Otodo. Some can easily support it. All it takes is one to take this thought to the family...</div> </div> </div> </div>Someone described the whole teaching through fear to be self-serving nonsense, and it should probably be so in a Hunter campaign, with the alliance being in the Beasts' minds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T01:38:49-07:00","id":562745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562441#post562441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562181#post562181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think Kenshi needs to be elaborated on, if that's the case, because the impression I got from references to talisman was that you're making a beat stick as opposed to forcing &quot;you must stand still&quot; on a demon; I suppose that means that the Birthright rank means you get more detailed restrictions, which does make sense (since you're able to customize it). Would someone be able to use a ban at a lower level (&quot;stay within this circle&quot; instead of &quot;explode when I look at you&quot;), in case they wanted to capture a yokai (&quot;where are you keeping them, monster?&quot;) It's actually a neat system. (Hey, look, explicit praise).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll clarify. But the primary intention would be to get them to stand still, or to otherwise restrain them (physically or in a more abstract sense). You could use it to make weapons or whatever? And yeah, you can use it at lower level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the most common form <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ofuda\" target=\"_blank\">ofuda</a> as in anime?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T01:40:14-07:00","id":562746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562441#post562441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else have any input on Kaibutsu? I don't mind that change. Full turn but not denying Defense isn't a bad idea. (Although there's a sick part of me that wants to deny Defense as a funny way to poke fun at transformation sequences.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually didn't mind the transformation. IMO if you want to turn big and red you should do it <i>before</i> your opponent knows you're present. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562742#post562742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone described the whole teaching through fear to be self-serving nonsense, and it should probably be so in a Hunter campaign, with the alliance being in the Beasts' minds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's so much great potential in teaching outdated primordial lessons through fear. If someone has a disabled child it's because they're an evil person and the gods are punishing them. In primordial terms get them and their family away from the gene pool. Cold logic that might have been necessary in the stone age, but it was evil then and it's even more evil now society has the resources and technology to support disabled children.<br /> <br /> (The related idea of shunning anti-vaxers is more justifiable, but only if you don't hurt the kids as well. I'm not sure if you can weild fear with that kind of precision, the law's a blunt instrument but fear is blunter still. And of course, it's only justifiable if anti-vaxers are wrong, the WoD is full of Conspiracies so they might be correct in setting.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 06-21-2015, 04:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T02:06:27-07:00","id":562751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562746#post562746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's so much great potential in teaching outdated primordial lessons through fear. If someone has a disabled child it's because they're an evil person and the gods are punishing them. In primordial terms get them and their family away from the gene pool. Cold logic that might have been necessary in the stone age, but it was evil then and it's even more evil now society has the resources and technology to support disabled children.<br /> <br /> (The related idea of shunning anti-vaxers is more justifiable, but only if you don't hurt the kids as well. I'm not sure if you can weild fear with that kind of precision, the law's a blunt instrument but fear is blunter still. And of course, it's only justifiable if anti-vaxers are wrong, the WoD is full of Conspiracies so they might be correct in setting.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind the evil part, but there seems to be an undercurrent that the Beasts are the good guys, doing people a favor through fear. In a Hunter campaign there should be Beasts doing primordial lessons that are evil like you say, as well as ones just using it as a justification for feeding their hunger.<br /> <br /> (I got a quickly reversed ban when I pointed out that W:tA's Magadon pretty much follows the anti-vaxxer position, with every medicine from them, explicitly including vaccines, is Wyrm-tainted.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T02:51:34-07:00","id":562776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562751#post562751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind the evil part, but there seems to be an undercurrent that the Beasts are the good guys, doing people a favor through fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the perspective of their own gameline they are. But you don't have to change anything for that to not be true anymore from a different moral vantage point. I mean hell, have you read how Beasts feed their hungers?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T03:37:38-07:00","id":562844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562776#post562776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the perspective of their own gameline they are. But you don't have to change anything for that to not be true anymore from a different moral vantage point. I mean hell, have you read how Beasts feed their hungers?!</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be getting revised, looking at the update for the <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/beast-the-primordial-prestige-edition/posts/1267487\" target=\"_blank\">Eshmaki</a>. However, I still can't imagine any Hunter group having cordial relations with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1460-tau-neutrino","name":"Tau Neutrino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1460_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T05:05:11-07:00","id":562862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562746#post562746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's so much great potential in teaching outdated primordial lessons through fear. If someone has a disabled child it's because they're an evil person and the gods are punishing them. In primordial terms get them and their family away from the gene pool. Cold logic that might have been necessary in the stone age, but it was evil then and it's even more evil now society has the resources and technology to support disabled children.</div> </div> </div> </div> Evil then? Lets not try to push universal morality on any culture, let alone one that developed under far less priviledged circumstances. Especially when such taboo things develop as survival requirements.<br /> <br /> In modern terms, American prisons don't work. In theory, we had this idea that we could rehabilitate criminals - its not true. You need over 40 years of therapy to correct somone in their prime on the easy cases. Prisons are filled with repeat offenders who flat out need to be removed from society. As welll, prisons are being treated as a cure-all, for people that shouldn't be in there. There are entire communities that refuse to deal with the police at all, even if there one lived next door to a serial killer. The no snitching rule is upheld by even law abiding, good hearted people that have no fear of criminal retribution.<br /> <br /> The simple truth of the matter is that many communities still, in this day and age, even in first world countries, police their own. Moral Beasts are no worse than we already do to ourselves, and may even be better in a lot of cases. Immoral Beasts... Well, they aren't worse than what some humans do to each other. Punishment is a necessary part of our society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T05:09:00-07:00","id":562863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562844#post562844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems to be getting revised, looking at the update for the <a href=\"http://&quot;https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/beast-the-primordial-prestige-edition/posts/1267487&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Eshmaki</a>. However, I still can't imagine any Hunter group having cordial relations with them.</div> </div> </div> </div> that depends all on contact, doesn't it? The vigilante vibe works well against the excess of supernaturals as well as mortals. So, the &quot;good&quot; Beasts can effectively hunt the bad. Beasts do end up on the bad side of monsters.<br /> <br /> Perfect situation for a sympathetic Otodo and Beast to meet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T05:12:03-07:00","id":562864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562745#post562745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the most common form <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ofuda\" target=\"_blank\">ofuda</a> as in anime?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't see why not. <br /> <br /> That said, I didn't call it out specifically because I'm almost certain I've already referenced Ofuda in something. I just can't remember off the top of my head. Maybe Kigan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T05:15:48-07:00","id":562870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562862#post562862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Evil then? Lets not try to push universal morality on any culture, let alone one that developed under far less priviledged circumstances. Especially when such taboo things develop as survival requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div> Speak for yourself. I think banishing people because they fall ill is a universal wrong. It might be nessecary; but that doesn't make it right.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:27:15-07:00","id":563604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=562870#post562870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Speak for yourself. I think banishing people because they fall ill is a universal wrong. It might be nessecary; but that doesn't make it right.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>are you saying they shouldn't do it and the entire village should die with him, or are you saying that they should do it, but it still counts as morally wrong (I.e. A literal necessary evil)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T00:54:26-07:00","id":563799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=563604#post563604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or are you saying that they should do it, but it still counts as morally wrong (I.e. A literal necessary evil)?</div> </div> </div> </div>This one. (Obviously that assumes banishing them is actually necessary.)<br /> <br /> If they chose to care for the sick and die on a matter of principle (literally impossible if the village contains children too young to give informed consent) then I take my hat off to them; but I don't think I could live up to such nobility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:49:38-07:00","id":564946,"title":"","content":"Just thinking about it, but since Kanabou Tetsubou are two handed, shouldn't it get 9-again?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T20:58:36-07:00","id":564971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=564946#post564946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just thinking about it, but since Kanabou Tetsubou are two handed, shouldn't it get 9-again?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it should. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T22:05:18-07:00","id":566096,"title":"","content":"I did a response on the blog, but maybe it's better here, so I'll repeat myself if nobody minds...<br /> <br /> The Otodo seem pretty interesting, and I'd look forward to using them. That said, what with &quot;dark bloodline&quot;, &quot;burning blood in their veins&quot;, and &quot;unholy birthright&quot; in a Japanese context, I can't help but think <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love,_Chunibyo_%26_Other_Delusions\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Chuunibyou&quot;</a> and wonder if there will be a lot of eyepatches. <br /> <br /> Anyway, someone on the blog side was mentioning that \u201cSeitokuken\u201d isn't really a common Japanese term. I just remember how &quot;majutsu&quot; &quot;\u9b54\u8853&quot; is usually used interchangeably with &quot;magic&quot;, but actually contains the character for &quot;demon&quot; in the first half. Some fantasy games, especially in the line of Dragon Quest parodies, tend to make a distinction between &quot;Holy Power&quot; as a good, oppositional force to the always-demon-related &quot;Magic&quot;. By that extension, you could go for the fairly literal, &quot;\u9b3c\u8853&quot; &quot;Kijutsu&quot;, which is literally &quot;Oni Techniques&quot;, but generally basically means sorcery. Alternately, there's &quot;\u9b3c\u6280&quot; &quot;oni-wara&quot;, which means something similar, and if you want to get away from overtly saying it's an oni, &quot;\u9b3c\u8840\u8853&quot; &quot;Oni-chijutsu&quot; is &quot;Oni-blood technique&quot;, which I don't think exists as a term in Japanese, but would likely be something you could pass off if you explained it.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I also have to mention I'd be more than a bit bummed if there weren't any way to play Buddhist priest or Shinto Miko conspiracies. I linked <a href=\"https://nirc.nanzan-u.ac.jp/nfile/750\" target=\"_blank\">this pdf in a previous thread</a>, as an example, but basically, you could lay the groundwork for a state-sponsored exorcist division. It could have room for both exploring actual historical religious practices, but also it would let me get a few anime-loving friends into playing this game if I convince them that it's basically playing a game of Inuyasha or Touhou or Kekkaishi with more historic connotations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T22:22:36-07:00","id":566121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=566096#post566096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a response on the blog, but maybe it's better here, so I'll repeat myself if nobody minds...<br /> <br /> The Otodo seem pretty interesting, and I'd look forward to using them. That said, what with &quot;dark bloodline&quot;, &quot;burning blood in their veins&quot;, and &quot;unholy birthright&quot; in a Japanese context, I can't help but think <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love,_Chunibyo_%26_Other_Delusions\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Chuunibyou&quot;</a> and wonder if there will be a lot of eyepatches.<br /> <br /> Anyway, someone on the blog side was mentioning that \u201cSeitokuken\u201d isn't really a common Japanese term. I just remember how &quot;majutsu&quot; &quot;\u9b54\u8853&quot; is usually used interchangeably with &quot;magic&quot;, but actually contains the character for &quot;demon&quot; in the first half. Some fantasy games, especially in the line of Dragon Quest parodies, tend to make a distinction between &quot;Holy Power&quot; as a good, oppositional force to the always-demon-related &quot;Magic&quot;. By that extension, you could go for the fairly literal, &quot;\u9b3c\u8853&quot; &quot;Kijutsu&quot;, which is literally &quot;Oni Techniques&quot;, but generally basically means sorcery. Alternately, there's &quot;\u9b3c\u6280&quot; &quot;oni-wara&quot;, which means something similar, and if you want to get away from overtly saying it's an oni, &quot;\u9b3c\u8840\u8853&quot; &quot;Oni-chijutsu&quot; is &quot;Oni-blood technique&quot;, which I don't think exists as a term in Japanese, but would likely be something you could pass off if you explained it.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I also have to mention I'd be more than a bit bummed if there weren't any way to play Buddhist priest or Shinto Miko conspiracies. I linked <a href=\"https://nirc.nanzan-u.ac.jp/nfile/750\" target=\"_blank\">this pdf in a previous thread</a>, as an example, but basically, you could lay the groundwork for a state-sponsored exorcist division. It could have room for both exploring actual historical religious practices, but also it would let me get a few anime-loving friends into playing this game if I convince them that it's basically playing a game of Inuyasha or Touhou or Kekkaishi with more historic connotations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never read those light novels, so I couldn't say? <br /> <br /> Seitokuken isn't a particularly common Japanese term in modern usage. That's kind of the point. Like Protean and Vicissitude aren't common usage English. I feel it helps with game terms. <br /> <br /> I'll see what I can do about Miko. I'd have to come up with something sort of unexpected there, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T22:42:47-07:00","id":566137,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Well, in that PDF, it has the following:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Tamura Hachiday\u016b\u2019s history and the control of <i>miko</i></b> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">According to a 1684 document penned by Tamura Hachiday\u016b\u2019s occupational precursor K\u014dwaka Kanday\u016b \u5e78\u82e5\u52d8\u592a\u592b (or K\u014dmatsu Kanday\u016b</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">\u5e78\u677e\u52d8\u592a\u592b; the name K\u014dwaka may have been merely an \u201cartist\u2019s name\u201d), the latter\u2019s ancestor had received an official \u201cvermillion-seal certificate\u201d during the sixth month 1618 from none other than Tokugawa Ieyasu (who had in fact died in 1616). This weighty license supposedly granted Kanday\u016b control of the \u201cdance masters\u201d (mai-day\u016b) and female \u201ccatalpa-bow shamans\u201d (azusa miko) of the eight Kant\u014d provinces, over 600 people in all (Hayashi 1993, 3; for a 1790 listing of villages and number of houses see Hayashi 2003, 64\u201365). Records from 1800 identify the initial recipient of Ieyasu\u2019s largesse as K\u014dmatsu Kan\u2019emon \u5e78\u677e\u52d8\u53f3\u885b\u9580 ; supposedly his son called himself Kanday\u016b. Kan\u2019emon had apparently arrived from Mikawa Province, the ancestral home of the Tokugawa family. Once in Edo, he was allegedly granted a plot of land at Tawara-ch\u014d and permitted to supervise the \u201cdance masters\u201d of Edo and the Kant\u014d provinces (Matsudaira 1942, 614).</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Again, I think you could set up a secret state-sponsored (or possibly not really state-sponsored, and built upon a forged signature of a dead Shogun - OR WAS HE REALLY DEAD?!) conspiracy using a concept like that. </span></span><br /> <br /> (The rest of the text goes on to talk about how it was basically a lot of infighting over which favored factions got control over specific branches of the religion, and who got the right to sell specific religious charms at different festivals, but that's just the official history... Multiple rival political families vying for rights over religious factions, whose members were generally fairly fluid, and could shift allegiances to suit their own needs, itself, is something fairly suited to WoD, as well. One group, but the different sub-factions are controlled by rival political families, and are only officially allowed specific rituals.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 06-24-2015, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T23:37:07-07:00","id":566146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=566137#post566137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[FONT=serif][SIZE=17px]Well, in that PDF, it has the following:<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Again, I think you could set up a secret state-sponsored (or possibly not really state-sponsored, and built upon a forged signature of a dead Shogun - OR WAS HE REALLY DEAD?!) conspiracy using a concept like that. </span></span><br /> <br /> (The rest of the text goes on to talk about how it was basically a lot of infighting over which favored factions got control over specific branches of the religion, and who got the right to sell specific religious charms at different festivals, but that's just the official history... Multiple rival political families vying for rights over religious factions, whose members were generally fairly fluid, and could shift allegiances to suit their own needs, itself, is something fairly suited to WoD, as well. One group, but the different sub-factions are controlled by rival political families, and are only officially allowed specific rituals.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome. Thank you for the share. I'm going to read this. Sounds neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T06:47:53-07:00","id":566305,"title":"","content":"just a random thought about the Hototogisu- what are the chances that in order to replicate the powers of other monsters they do some.. human experimentation? I don't know why, but I have a sudden urge for seeing such a group in WoD (not including Cheiron. That's not experimentation. it's pure business)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T15:12:05-07:00","id":567050,"title":"","content":"Reading it again, one of the other interesting things that is in the &quot;Female Shamans in Eastern Japan&quot; excerpt is that they mention regulations encouraging/enforcing that they intermarry with onmyouji and yamabushi. Presumably in real life, this could be as part of an enforcement of caste that was a huge part of Edo, but since magical powers were supposed to be based upon bloodline, (especially through relations with some sort of divine or divinely-sponsored magical creature,) you could say a similar preservation of magical powers was in effect. <br /> <br /> Although it's lower on my personal wishlist than miko and bhikku hunter squads, one of the things about yamabushi is that tengu, in their not-always-evil mythological roles, are often associated with yamabushi. (One very prominent story has a tengu that takes the form of a human to learn their branch of ascetic Buddhism, and in general, they are portrayed as wearing a yamabushi's clothes from then on whenever they aren't the automatically-evil sorts...) Very broadly speaking, I prefer it when the non-humans aren't Always Chaotic Evil, as there's far more storytelling potential for them when one can't be excused for just shooting them first.<br /> <br /> ===<br /> <br /> Also, to go back to a previous topic that Aspel brought up again, but the backstory on how the oni created a bunch of oni-blooded children really does have the vibe of, &quot;Boy meets monster. Five minutes later, freaky interspecies sex!&quot; Considering how saturated Japanese folklore (and its modern anime interpretations) are with monsters that pretty much overtly are either false-face seductive women or brutes out to &quot;steal our women&quot;, (and oni have been both,) it really does beg the question why this one village is the <i>only</i> time such a union ever occurred. Even if we take this as just straight-up a copy-paste of the Lucifuge into another culture, even in the Lucifuge, it reads as the devil manages to <i>keep</i> on getting around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T15:38:47-07:00","id":567071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=567050#post567050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, to go back to a previous topic that Aspel brought up again, but the backstory on how the oni created a bunch of oni-blooded children really does have the vibe of, &quot;Boy meets monster. Five minutes later, freaky interspecies sex!&quot; Considering how saturated Japanese folklore (and its modern anime interpretations) are with monsters that pretty much overtly are either false-face seductive women or brutes out to &quot;steal our women&quot;, (and oni have been both,) it really does beg the question why this one village is the <i>only</i> time such a union ever occurred. Even if we take this as just straight-up a copy-paste of the Lucifuge into another culture, even in the Lucifuge, it reads as the devil manages to <i>keep</i> on getting around.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not necessarily the only time such a union ever occurred. It's the only time a whole village made that decision. <br /> <br /> Could there be other oni babies out there? Sure. They're just not abundant enough, with enough shared history to group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T16:24:16-07:00","id":567109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=567071#post567071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not necessarily the only time such a union ever occurred. It's the only time a whole village made that decision.<br /> <br /> Could there be other oni babies out there? Sure. They're just not abundant enough, with enough shared history to group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, is it really so important to the group that it all be just one (fairly inbred) family? They could just as well be tracking down a string of interspecies relations. Not making it a unique event means you don't need to explain why that one nameless village is the only time it ever occurred or will occur. If you want one village to be the central source, it begs the question why only those villagers were either desperate or desirous enough to be the only people to try... and there have been plenty of extremely desperate people willing to do anything from sell their families into slavery to cannibalism in history. <br /> <br /> Alternately, if there are oni-blooded people being born, but they're excluded from Hunter Club, why is the new blood turned down, or more likely, hunted down? Especially if it says in the text that their blood is getting thin, it would seem an obvious solution to just circulate some of that fresher blood around. <br /> <br /> Making it an ongoing problem to have shape-changing oni seducers and secret offspring that may inherit positions of power, or oni that take over villages and demand mates would also be a natural starting point for storyhooks...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T16:28:23-07:00","id":567113,"title":"","content":"Part of the goal of the Otodo, from what I can gather, is that the group connects with the many small incidents around the country and brings them into the 'family'. Having a big kick off moment creates a central enough organization to provide resources and goals. In other words, the oni-orgy village is a snowball rolled down the mountain. The Otodo as it is by the time of the setting is probably a larger boulder of snow halfway down the mountain, and the Otodo in modern day is a mountain of ice unto itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-07-2015, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T17:19:44-07:00","id":567137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wraith_Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=567109#post567109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, is it really so important to the group that it all be just one (fairly inbred) family? They could just as well be tracking down a string of interspecies relations. Not making it a unique event means you don't need to explain why that one nameless village is the only time it ever occurred or will occur. If you want one village to be the central source, it begs the question why only those villagers were either desperate or desirous enough to be the only people to try... and there have been plenty of extremely desperate people willing to do anything from sell their families into slavery to cannibalism in history.<br /> <br /> Alternately, if there are oni-blooded people being born, but they're excluded from Hunter Club, why is the new blood turned down, or more likely, hunted down? Especially if it says in the text that their blood is getting thin, it would seem an obvious solution to just circulate some of that fresher blood around.<br /> <br /> Making it an ongoing problem to have shape-changing oni seducers and secret offspring that may inherit positions of power, or oni that take over villages and demand mates would also be a natural starting point for storyhooks...</div> </div> </div> </div>What Arc said. Additionally, there's a reason for it. It's a slightly oblique reference. I don't think anyone's caught it yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T17:59:26-07:00","id":567188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=567137#post567137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Arc said. Additionally, there's a reason for it. It's a slightly oblique reference. I don't think anyone's caught it yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm almost certainly wrong and about to make myself look like an idiot, but is it <i>The Shadow over Innsmouth</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T18:20:29-07:00","id":567209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=567188#post567188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm almost certainly wrong and about to make myself look like an idiot, but is it <i>The Shadow over Innsmouth</i>?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't look like an idiot. But nope. If anyone gets it, I'll be shocked. But it's Barker, not Lovecraft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T07:56:18-07:00","id":582289,"title":"","content":"Two questions David, and obviously understand if you can't/don't want to answer either yet...<br /> <br /> 1. Can you tell us the dates-range of the setting?<br /> <br /> 2. Are the archaic Hototogisu a Compact or Conspiracy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T08:44:10-07:00","id":582401,"title":"","content":"I think that the Hototogisu are a Conspiracy simply because it was said there are 3 compacts and 2 conspiracies- and the samurais, the escorts and the pearl divers are all described as Compacts, so elimination says they are a conspiracy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T17:19:48-07:00","id":582912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=582289#post582289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two questions David, and obviously understand if you can't/don't want to answer either yet...<br /> <br /> 1. Can you tell us the dates-range of the setting?<br /> <br /> 2. Are the archaic Hototogisu a Compact or Conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1640s. <br /> <br /> Conspiracy. While on the smaller end (sort of, in a weird subjective way), they have an Endowment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T00:55:57-07:00","id":583256,"title":"","content":"I'm really hoping Hunter 2ed fixes Endowment = Conspiracy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T01:27:09-07:00","id":583264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=583256#post583256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really hoping Hunter 2ed fixes Endowment = Conspiracy</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't like the distinction between the two. I think it's way too arbitrary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T08:56:07-07:00","id":583509,"title":"","content":"I don't have a problem with making the primary division between Hunter organization categories whether or not they have Endowments - that is a central &quot;feel&quot; issue that is going to impact theme and gameplay. But just don't pretend that has an association with size. Plenty of Endowment wielding groups are going to be small insular mystery cults. Plenty of groups without Endowments are going to be world-spanning networks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T09:22:30-07:00","id":583532,"title":"","content":"I'm going to say what I've always said on the subject- having supernatural powers doesn't mean you are a Conspiracy, and not having supernatural powers doesn't make you into a Compact. TF:V, for example, don't have supernatural powers- they are a Conspiracy with a very high tech weapons and devices, and so are the AKD who are &quot;just&quot; and ancient Conspiracy who has tons of Relics.<br /> <br /> Endowments are, the way I see it, a way to mechanically represent the collective knowledge a certain group (the Conspiracy) has gathered and made available to all of its agents of certain level of recognition (Status) which gives them a special edge upon both supernatural, mundane and vigilant threats and/or competitors. If that knowledge can't be replicated in an efficient way and be taught to all of the agents of the Conspiracy, then that knowledge is not an Endowment, just a supernatural or mundane advantage certain individuals in a certain group has.<br /> <br /> That means that being a Mystery Cult which has access to certain Supernatural Merits, and there are big organizations which do not have any kind of supernatural or mundane edge. Why? Because they are not hunters. The Compacts and Conspiracies of the hunters are focused around the Vigil, and the knowledge they gathered through their hunt is what makes their Endowment. I think that the reason some people think Endowments and Conspiracies should be broken apart from each other is because of two groups- the Lucifuge and the Promethean Brotherhood, which have their Endowment as their &quot;reason of existence&quot;. I don't think it's the right way to read them (that is, Castigations are not inborn abilities but rites which unleash the potential of the hunter and that the Rite of Hecate could be considered as a proper Endowment only when it is finalized), but I agree that they can cause some confusion. The Lucifuge also create that feeling because they have a limited number which sounds small- but Tiers are about the reach of the organization, and the Lucifuge has been detailed has having a 3rd tier reach through all the books.<br /> <br /> In short, the reason only Conspiracies have &quot;real Endowments&quot; (not including the C&amp;C ones) is because it is an easy way to mechanically represent old and powerful occult organizations. For a Compact, meeting someone with and Endowment like power should be terrifying. For a Conspiracy, it's what makes them terrifying.<br /> <br /> At least, that's how I've always viewed the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T09:44:38-07:00","id":583547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=583532#post583532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TF:V, for example, don't have supernatural powers</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they absolutely do. There is nothing &quot;realistic bleeding edge science&quot; about Etheric bullets. I'm not saying they didn't use the scienfic method to develop said tech, but it was the scientific method applied to supernatural phenomena with supernatural materials. A good portion of Advanced Armory is occult in nature.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">QUOTE=LostLight;n583532]</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That means that being a Mystery Cult which has access to certain Supernatural Merits, and there are big organizations which do not have any kind of supernatural or mundane edge. Why? Because they are not hunters.</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">[/QUOTE]</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Then First Edition's definition of Hunter groups is restrained to the point of ridiculousness.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A &quot;Compact&quot; can span the world via internet networking with thousands upon thousands of members, and still not have the infrastructure necessary to produce or wield potent Endowments like those of the Canon Conspiracies. A small hierarchical group of extremely dedicated Hunters can have unique Occult abilities due to some ancient oath their the heirs of.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:11:27-07:00","id":583561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=583547#post583547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes they absolutely do. There is nothing &quot;realistic bleeding edge science&quot; about Etheric bullets. I'm not saying they didn't use the scienfic method to develop said tech, but it was the scientific method applied to supernatural phenomena with supernatural materials. A good portion of Advanced Armory is occult in nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, by the strange rules of RPG definitions of magic and technology, Etheric Bullets are the most technology-like piece of equipment available.<br /> <br /> While the philosophy of fantasy/sci-fi has always been &quot;Any sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic, and any sufficiently analyzed magic is indistinguishable from technology,&quot; in RPGs, the difference has been one of transferability. Magic is a property of the wielder, while technology is the property of their equipment. Wizards rely upon inherent magic powers, while fighters can trade the magical powers of their equipment with any other fighter they run across. The space marine's plasma gun is usable by anyone with working opposable thumbs, but the psychic's powers are innate and cannot be transferred. Even magic artifacts are distinguishable from technological tools by their (lack of) mass reproduction. Magic is a special snowflake. Technology makes us all fungible. Tone aside, their results are the same.<br /> <br /> Etheric rounds are only purchasable/requisitionable by Valkyrie, but any random yahoo that gets a clip can jam it into a gun they bought at WalMart and cap some ghosts. Their bleeder and lightning guns, meanwhile, <i>refuse to function</i> for anyone but their specified masters, making them an innate, non-transferable part of the character who purchased them. Comparatively, Aegis Kai Doru relics are transferable (although story reasons would make one not want to) to the point that the only thing &quot;special&quot; about any given character is admittance to magic club, while alchemy from the Ascending Ones is only transferable to another Ascending One of equal or greater endowment dots, but the bleeder gun that a TF:V character has can't be used by any other TF:V character in a way that makes it equivalent to one of the prosthetics of Chieron.<br /> <br /> ---------<br /> <br /> Anyway, as for the distinction between compact and conspiracy, I think it may be better to take the path glamourweaver talked about, and take the implication of size away from a conspiracy. So far as game effects go, the difference of making one group have a superpower, and another group not having one is simple and clear enough a dividing line. Inversely, size is sketchy and always ill-defined for storyteller flexibility purposes, anyway (barring Lucifuge). It also may have little to really do with the themes of the game. (How impotant is it whether The Union has equal distribution around the world versus small pockets around the world with a few clusters of concentration in the Rustbelt, versus nowhere outside the Rustbelt if you're playing the whole game in Chicago?)<br /> <br /> A conspiracy, technically, is just more than one person, anyway, and it can mean any group that has some secret. Use the difference in tiers to mean something like &quot;Some random guys who REALLY don't know what they're getting into&quot; -&gt; &quot;A group organized enough to understand enough to be dangerous and not get wiped out so fast they can learn from their mistakes&quot; -&gt; &quot;A group deep in enough that they're gaining monster powers, themselves, but who now have a much stronger reason to keep others out.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5120,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","user":"Wraith_Magus","date":". 07-08-2015, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T16:18:10-07:00","id":583972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=583264#post583264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don't like the distinction between the two. I think it's way too arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. Which is why I'm hoping that 2E will clearly define what the distinction between a Compact and a Conspiracy is.<br /> <br /> IMO a Compact should be that you have access to a network of like minded hunters who'll share information and resources; but you're still mostly a free agent. A Conspiracy means you're not a free agent, somebody gives you orders and you obey them* but you get all the benefits organisation can bring: More resources, more information, more backup; the simple fact that you can organise a raid on every branch of a vampire's network at the same time.<br /> <br /> Sometimes a Compact has a powerful supernatural Endowment. Sometimes a Conspiracy has no Endowment.<br /> <br /> *Unless you have enough Status. Then you're giving the orders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=583509#post583509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a problem with making the primary division between Hunter organization categories whether or not they have Endowments - that is a central &quot;feel&quot; issue that is going to impact theme and gameplay. But just don't pretend that has an association with size. Plenty of Endowment wielding groups are going to be small insular mystery cults. Plenty of groups without Endowments are going to be world-spanning networks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think wheather or not you're getting orders from the chain of command would have more effect on the central &quot;feel&quot; than wheather or not you're Endowed.<br /> <br /> But ultimately I don't care too much what's the &quot;primary&quot; division. I just want the tangle between Endowments, Tier, size of the organisation, and structure of the organisation to be untangled.<br /> <br /> I'd like Compact and Conspiracy to be defined as above; because I think it's a logical division point and because tying the words to Endowments is linguistically weird and there's no need for a special keyword to say Endowments are present. You can just look at the Endowment section.<br /> <br /> But so long as the tangle is untangled and significantly more attention is paid to how groups organise themselves I'd be happy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=583547#post583547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A &quot;Compact&quot; can span the world via internet networking with thousands upon thousands of members, and still not have the infrastructure necessary to produce or wield potent Endowments like those of the Canon Conspiracies. A small hierarchical group of extremely dedicated Hunters can have unique Occult abilities due to some ancient oath their the heirs of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always considered the AKD to be larger than Net0 if you only count active hunters. Significantly larger if you count support personal and pawns; but significantly smaller if you count Net0's non-contributing viewers.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T00:05:11-07:00","id":584337,"title":"","content":"I really like Kigo as a power.<br /> <br /> I can imagine some ancient evil, stamped with dozens of unique Kanji across their aura from years of scrapes and encounters with Otodo. While an Integrity-based pool is harsh, I do have a question: Can you only do this once or are you capable of slapstick-animeing it up by smashing some unfortunate youkai or whatnot with dozens of kanji?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T01:29:29-07:00","id":584387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=584337#post584337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like Kigo as a power.<br /> <br /> I can imagine some ancient evil, stamped with dozens of unique Kanji across their aura from years of scrapes and encounters with Otodo. While an Integrity-based pool is harsh, I do have a question: Can you only do this once or are you capable of slapstick-animeing it up by smashing some unfortunate youkai or whatnot with dozens of kanji?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm going to be limiting it to a single use per victim. I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:32:58-07:00","id":584770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/560314-new-conspiracy-the-otodo?p=584337#post584337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like Kigo as a power.<br /> <br /> I can imagine some ancient evil, stamped with dozens of unique Kanji across their aura from years of scrapes and encounters with Otodo. While an Integrity-based pool is harsh, I do have a question: Can you only do this once or are you capable of slapstick-animeing it up by smashing some unfortunate youkai or whatnot with dozens of kanji?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm getting mental images of Skuld from Oh! My Goddess, here...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T13:51:59-07:00","id":585134,"title":"","content":"Now that i have seen it in actual play, my general hypothesis that Otodo are SAVAGE has been proved correct. Note, if you are playing with mortals, one of your party members will probably run off when you turn into oni-form with Kaibutsu. Second Note: because you want a really high willpower, you will not fail a lot of breaking points and get a number of exceptional successes on breaking points (the Otodo character in game has yet to get a negative condition) you are in near Garou form but with more flexibility (hmm, Imma just take this +5 Strength thanks) So all told, i really like them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}